{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghJzhJimTgo3KX3kV7Rh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01C7WsXRFtDvcq1jjKyQYkUx","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261103-220909__x5b1962/work/PLAN.md","offset":430,"limit":200},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1855,"cache_read_input_tokens":85434,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1855},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7a314112-273a-4f48-a672-e1ae4461860d","uuid":"af74e7fe-f089-4277-92e7-f2b1ca8add5b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T05:09:40.385Z","request_id":"req_011CghJzh36hFy8xyNEuPdkF","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01C7WsXRFtDvcq1jjKyQYkUx":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261103-220909__x5b1962/work/PLAN.md","offset":430,"limit":200}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C7WsXRFtDvcq1jjKyQYkUx","type":"tool_result","content":"430\t### 6.5 Items, bag, hotbar, chests\n431\t- **Bag:** 40 slots, stacks of 99. Key items are separate and unlimited.\n432\t- **Hotbar:** 8 slots that reference item ids in the bag, DQB style. A count of 0 shows a greyed slot. Pickups fill an empty hotbar slot with new placeable or usable items.\n433\t- **Pickups:** broken blocks and defeated monsters drop item entities that bounce out, bob and spin. After 0.3 s they magnetize to a builder within 1.5 blocks and are auto-picked with a \"pickup\" blip. A toast shows \"+3 Straw\" (stacked toasts, bottom right). If the bag is full, the drop stays and the toast says \"Your bag is full!\". Drops despawn after 5 minutes.\n434\t- **Chests:** 20 slots. Interact opens a two-pane screen (bag | chest) with \"Store all materials\".\n435\t- **Town Chest:** from Town Level 2, any chest inside the border can be made the Town Chest (interact → \"Make this the Town Chest\"). Residents put gifts in and take materials out of it for Patterns, and Marigold cooks from it. Exactly one Town Chest exists.\n436\t\n437\t### 6.6 Crafting, stations, Notions\n438\t- **Stations:** Pocket (from the Bag tab \"Pocket Notions\"), Mending Bench, Hearth Pot, Thimble Forge. A station screen lists known recipes for that station.\n439\t  - Each row: icon, name, and ingredients as icons with have/need counts. Have ≥ need shows white with a tick icon, otherwise red with a cross icon (counts in text too, never colour alone). The pixel font has no ✓ or ✗, so draw them as `DQ.Glyphs` icons.\n440\t  - Quantity picker ×1, ×5 or Max. Confirm crafts.\n441\t  - At most 6 rows per page. A large detail pane shows the description.\n442\t- **Crafting feedback:** the builder hammers at the station (a `bash` loop for 0.5 s), sparkles fly, a \"ta-da\" chime plays, and the item's icon pops above the station. Crafted items go into the bag.\n443\t- **Notions** (inspiration). Each recipe has `notion: { on: 'pickup'|'quest'|'level'|'talk'|'start', key }`. The first time the trigger fires:\n444\t  1. The recipe unlocks.\n445\t  2. The builder strikes a thinking pose (a `kneel` blend for 0.4 s, then `'cheer'`).\n446\t  3. A thought bubble shows the item icon above the head for 2 s.\n447\t  4. A harp-gliss jingle plays.\n448\t  5. The popup reads \"**You've got a notion!** Straw Bed. Craft it at a Mending Bench.\"\n449\t  - Popups queue and never overlap.\n450\t  - The Journal's Notions page lists all known recipes.\n451\t\n452\t### 6.7 Objects\n453\tData is in §7.5. Behaviour:\n454\t- **Doors** (2 levels high, 1 cell): they swing open with a tween when a builder or resident is within 1 cell, and close after they leave. Monsters treat closed doors as walls and attack them (door HP 30/50). A broken door drops nothing and breaks the room.\n455\t- **Lights** (torch, lantern, Glow Patch, hearth, forge, banner): each frame, add `game.lights.add(x, y, z+12, radius, intensity, { color })` for lights within the view plus 2 cells. Torch flames come from the engine's shape `flames`. Torches count as room lights.\n456\t- **Beds:** interact at night (19:00–05:00) with no monster within 8 blocks: fade to black, a \"Zzz\" jingle, and time jumps to 06:00. HP is restored, Belly −10, and an autosave runs. During the day: \"It's not bedtime yet!\" Residents use beds at night (§6.10).\n457\t- **Stations:** interact opens crafting. A station must be inside the town border to count for rooms; it works anywhere.\n458\t- **Pin Trap:** a floor object. Monsters on it take 8 damage every 0.8 s and are slowed ×0.6. Builders and residents are unharmed.\n459\t- **Bobbin Ballista** (HP 150):\n460\t  - Unmanned: during a siege it auto-fires at the nearest regular monster within 10 blocks every 5 s (20 damage); it never targets bosses.\n461\t  - Manned (interact):\n462\t    1. The builder sits behind it and the camera eases toward the ballista's facing.\n463\t    2. Stick or mouse aims within ±60°, with aim-assist snapping to the nearest monster in a 12° cone.\n464\t    3. □/LMB fires a spool bolt: 260 u/s, 30 damage, pierces 1. It counts as a *Tangle hit* on Gnarlgrim.\n465\t    4. Reload takes 2.5 s (a crank animation plus a click-clack).\n466\t    5. ○ dismounts.\n467\t  - When destroyed it becomes a \"Broken Ballista\". Interact with 2 Planks to repair it fully.\n468\t- **Bobbin Portals** (prebuilt at POIs): touching one *discovers* it (a jingle and \"Portal attuned: Corduroy Crags\"). Interact opens a travel list of discovered portals: a swirl transition to the destination, ending in front of that portal.\n469\t- **Plants** (tufts, cotton puffs, berry bushes, flowers, puffballs, dead bushes): object-plants that break in one hit with any tool and drop items (§7.3). They regrow at their original spot after 1 in-game day if the cell is still free.\n470\t- **Ancient Buttons** (S3 collectibles): big golden button objects that glint. Interact to collect.\n471\t- **The Banner of Mending:** interact opens the Banner screen: town name, level, a Cheer bar to the next level, the room list, residents and their mood, and the next unlock.\n472\t\n473\t### 6.8 Rooms (`DQ.Rooms`)\n474\t**The rule** (as in the source): a room is an enclosed floor area of **2 to 64 cells**, surrounded on every side by walls **at least 2 blocks high**. It must have **at least one door** in its perimeter and **at least one light** inside. A roof is optional. The room must be inside the town border to count for Cheer, but rooms are detected anywhere so the HUD can say \"Rooms only count inside the town border!\"\n475\t\n476\t**Algorithm** (debounced 0.3 s after any `blockPlaced`, `blockBroken`, `objectPlaced` or `objectRemoved` inside the border + 2 cells):\n477\t1. Collect candidate floor levels L in the region: levels where a cell has solid(L−1) and air at L and L+1, or an object at L that is not a door.\n478\t2. For each L, classify every cell in the region:\n479\t   - WALL: opaque solid blocks at both L and L+1.\n480\t   - DOOR: a door object at L, set in a straight wall: the two cells beside it along the wall are WALL or DOOR. A door on a corner does not count.\n481\t   - FLOOR: not solid at L and L+1, solid below, an object allowed.\n482\t   - OPEN: anything else, including low walls of 1 block and void.\n483\t3. Flood-fill FLOOR cells (4-connected). A component is a room if it:\n484\t   - never reaches an OPEN cell, a region edge or the border;\n485\t   - has a size of 2–64;\n486\t   - touches ≥ 1 DOOR;\n487\t   - contains ≥ 1 light object.\n488\t4. Classify it by the objects on its cells against `DQ.ROOMS`, in priority order. The first match wins; otherwise it is a **Snug**.\n489\t5. Match it to the previous room set by cell overlap ≥ 70%. Emit `roomFormed` (new, or its type changed) and `roomLost`.\n490\t6. **Cheer** is awarded the first time a room of each type forms in a \"slot\". A room's identity is its type plus a hash of its rounded centre, so rebuilding the same room does not pay again; each type pays at most `maxAwards` times (§7.6).\n491\t7. On `roomFormed`: a big centred banner (\"ROOM COMPLETE! Bedroom\") in stitched letters, a fanfare jingle, confetti scraps over the room, and a room-name label floating over its centre for 3 s. Residents react with `cheer` poses.\n492\t\n493\tThe overlay \"Dev → Show rooms\" tints room cells by type and shows OPEN leak cells in red with a cross icon. Use it to explain failures.\n494\t\n495\t**Leak hints:** when a nearly enclosed area fails, the builder looks at the Banner screen or uses Builder's Eye over it. The HUD names the first missing requirement: \"Missing: a door\" / \"a light\" / \"walls must be 2 blocks high\" / \"too big (max 64)\".\n496\t\n497\t### 6.9 Town: Banner, border, Cheer, levels, Patterns (`DQ.Town`)\n498\t- **Planting.** Use the Banner on the marked plaza spot in Thimbleton. That runs a cutscene: the banner rises, a golden light ring expands, and the **border stitch** runs around the town square.\n499\t  - The border is a square of side `2r+1` around the banner, with `r` from §7.7.\n500\t  - On the ground it is an animated dashed running stitch (cream thread, 2-px dashes moving along the edge), drawn at each border cell's surface height.\n501\t  - In the void, at night, it glows faintly.\n502\t- **Cheer sources:** rooms (§7.6), quest rewards, and Cheer bubbles from residents (+5 each, §6.10).\n503\t  - Collecting a bubble: it flies to the HUD banner icon, which pulses, with a two-note \"ding\".\n504\t  - On reaching a level threshold:\n505\t    1. Town Level up (a cutscene of about 4 s): the banner glows, a new stripe stitches itself onto it, and the border grows outward in an animated sweep.\n506\t    2. A popup lists the unlocks.\n507\t    3. The Lv-up jingle plays.\n508\t    4. The next resident arrives at the following dawn (or immediately if it is daytime, walking in from the east road).\n509\t- **Patterns** (blueprints):\n510\t  - **Pattern data:** `{ id, name, size:[w,d,h], layers: [ASCII rows per level], legend: { ch: blockKey | {obj, facing} }, reward }`.\n511\t  - **Placement:** the player uses a Pattern scroll (key item) and a ghost footprint follows the cursor. Turn it 90° with L1/R1 (pad), or the mouse wheel or [ / ] (keyboard); the camera still turns with Q/E and the right stick. Confirm on valid ground inside the border: flat ± 1 level, no objects in the way (blocks in the way are OK; they are shown as \"remove\").\n512\t  - **Ghosts:** each unbuilt cell draws a translucent ghost of its target block (`px.blend(.35)`) with a dashed outline; wrong blocks get a red cross icon. The HUD shows a panel: \"Quilters' Hall: 37/129\", then the materials still needed (have/need, e.g. Cobble 12/35).\n513\t  - **Building:** placing the right block into a ghost cell counts it, with a sparkle and a short arpeggio. Objects in ghost cells (door, lanterns) count the same way.\n514\t  - **Helpers:** residents with the `helper` job (Professor, Wren, and Mortimer by day) take the needed materials from the Town Chest. Each walks to an unbuilt ghost cell they can reach and places a block with a hammer animation and a \"tok\". Rate: `tuning.helperRate` blocks/min each (default 6). If the chest lacks materials, they say so in a balloon (\"Need Planks!\") and idle.\n515\t  - **Completion:** when every cell matches, a celebration cutscene plays (§7.10) and the reward and Cheer are granted. The structure counts as a special room (\"Quilters' Hall\") if its rules match (§7.6).\n516\t\n517\t### 6.10 Residents (`DQ.Residents`)\n518\t- Each resident is a `VoxelBody` plus a `Humanoid` or `Blob` rig, with a profile from `DQ.NPCS` (§7.8): `job`, `schedule`, `needs`, `voice`, `fighter` stats, and dialog nodes.\n519\t- **Schedule** (hours of the day clock; each block picks a target):\n520\t\n521\t  | Time | Activity |\n522\t  |---|---|\n523\t  | 06–08 | Wake, stretch (`wave` pose), go to the plaza |\n524\t  | 08–18 | Job: see below; between tasks, wander inside the border |\n525\t  | 18–20 | Supper: sit at a Mess Hall stool if one exists and eat (+bubble) |\n526\t  | 20–21 | Socialise near the Banner (talk balloons `note`, `dots`) |\n527\t  | 21–06 | Sleep in a free bed in a Bedroom (+bubble at 06:00); without one, sleep on the ground beside the Banner (mood −1, a \"No bed...\" balloon) |\n528\t- **Jobs:**\n529\t  - **Wren** (gatherer): each morning she puts 3 random basics (straw, branch, cotton) into the Town Chest. In sieges she uses a slingshot (4 damage, range 6 blocks, 1.2 s).\n530\t  - **Mortimer** (guard): patrols the border at night with a lantern and fights monsters inside the border with a club (8 damage, `overhead`). In sieges he leads the defence. He needs a Guard Post to stand watch from (+bubble).\n531\t  - **Marigold** (cook): with a Kitchen, cooks at the Hearth Pot (stirring loop) twice a day from Town Chest ingredients into the chest. At 18:00 she sets a dish on the Mess Hall table. In sieges she throws hot pies (5 damage, arc).\n532\t  - **Professor Selvage** (helper): builds Patterns from the Town Chest at the helper rate, or reads in the Workshop. In sieges he hides in the Hall.\n533\t  - **Lintwick** (fluff-farmer): puts 2 Lint into the Town Chest daily and dances (a Blob hop loop) when happy. In sieges he rolls into monsters (3 damage + knockback).\n534\t- **Needs and Cheer bubbles.** At most once per day per need, each satisfied need spawns a floating pink heart bubble (+5 Cheer) over the resident, which stays until collected:\n535\t  - sleep: slept in a bed\n536\t  - meal: ate a dish\n537\t  - comfort: their favourite room exists (Wren: Bedroom, Mortimer: Guard Post, Marigold: Kitchen, Professor: Workshop, Lintwick: a Bedroom with a Felt block in its walls)\n538\t\n539\t  Collect a bubble by walking within 2 blocks of it. Unhappy residents show a `dots` balloon and say why when you talk to them.\n540\t- **Requests:** a resident with an available quest shows a bouncing \"!\" balloon (`story.emote`). Talking starts it, and its steps appear in the Journal and HUD. When the steps are done, a \"?\" balloon shows; talk to them to turn it in.\n541\t- **Arrival cutscene:** the resident walks in along the east road, the camera pans to them, and they say their intro line. \"Mortimer has moved into Thimbleton!\" shows with a jingle.\n542\t- **Navigation** (`DQ.Nav`):\n543\t  - **Graph:** nodes are standable `(x, y, L)`. Edges:\n544\t    - 8-neighbour moves (diagonals only if both orthogonal neighbours are open), cost 1 (diagonal 1.41)\n545\t    - step up 1 level (a hop), cost 2\n546\t    - drop down 1–3 levels, cost 1.5\n547\t    - doors open for residents, closed for monsters\n548\t  - **A\\*** with a binary heap, capped at 3,000 expanded nodes. Smooth paths by line-of-walk. Re-path when an edit touches a path cell.\n549\t  - **Stuck rule:** if a resident has not progressed for 8 s and is off-screen, teleport them to the target. On screen, try a hop, then re-path.\n550\t- **Talk:** dialog with a portrait (`rig.drawPortrait`) and the resident's voice. Lines vary by flags, time of day, mood and town level (`E.Story` nodes with `if` conditions).\n551\t\n552\t### 6.11 Monsters and combat (`DQ.Monsters`, `DQ.Combat`)\n553\t- **AI states:** `idle/wander → notice` (a \"!\" over the head plus a squeak, 0.3 s) `→ chase → windup` (telegraph: flash, crouch or squash, a sound) `→ attack → recover`. Then `→ flee` (below 20% HP for Lintlings) or `→ hurt` (stagger 0.25 s) `→ dead` (pop, particles, drops, `monsterKilled`).\n554\t  - Aggro uses radius `tuning.aggro`, scaled by type (§7.9), plus `world.raycast` sight from eye height.\n555\t  - Leash: return home after chasing 24 blocks away from home.\n556\t- **Spawning:**\n557\t  - Region tables (§7.1) by day or night. Spawn on standable cells under open sky, ≥ 10 blocks from the builder, outside the town border, never inside rooms or during cutscenes.\n558\t  - Rate: 1 spawn per `tuning.spawnEvery` s (day 8, night 5) while the active count is below `tuning.maxMonsters` (default 10).\n559\t  - Despawn: more than 40 blocks away for 20 s.\n560\t- **Damage:**\n561\t  - `dmg = max(1, round((atk − def/2) × U(0.9, 1.1)))`, where U is drawn from the combat stream.\n562\t  - Builder crits: 5%, ×1.5 (Spin Stitch never crits).\n563\t  - Multipliers: `tuning.monsterHp`, `tuning.monsterDmg`, `tuning.builderAtk`, and difficulty (Relaxed 0.5 damage taken, Normal 1, Hard 1.4).\n564\t- **Hit feedback:**\n565\t  - `game.hitFx(x,y,z,{ power, damage, angle })` (hit-stop, shake, impact star, damage number), plus `E.knockback(builder, mon, 120, 40)`.\n566\t  - Monster hits on the builder: knockback 90, i-frames 0.8 s, a red vignette flash under `game.flash` limits.\n567\t  - Each move has its own sound.\n568\t- **Drops:** rolled on death from the drop table (`tuning.dropRate` multiplier on chances); items fly out.\n569\t\n570\t### 6.12 Siege and bosses (`DQ.Siege`, `DQ.Bosses`)\n571\t- **Siege director** (used once in the story, M13–M14, and in the Bee round). It is a `game.script` generator:\n572\t  1. **Prep.** Mortimer's rally line, then a 90 s countdown banner (\"The Knotted army approaches! 1:30\"). Build defences meanwhile; the music turns tense with the drum layer.\n573\t  2. **Autosave checkpoint** `siege`.\n574\t  3. **Waves** W1 → W2 → W3 (§7.9). Each wave spawns over 10 s from the east road (96,76), the Rift (96,80) and the north path (72,52). It ends when all of its monsters are defeated. Between waves: a 25 s breather with \"Wave cleared!\" and a repair prompt.\n575\t  4. **Boss.** Gnarlgrim enters through the Rift (cutscene, §7.10).\n576\t- **Monster targets in sieges:** first the Banner (HP 300; its HP bar is on the HUD during the siege), then ballistas, then the nearest town-structure block in the way (flagged `town` when placed inside the border), then residents, then the builder.\n577\t  - Monsters path with **breaker A\\***: wall blocks count as passable at cost 8 per block, and doors at cost 4.\n578\t  - On reaching a blocking block or door, a monster attacks it (Lintling 3, Pinhog 6, Frayed Knight 8, Knotbrute 25, Gnarlgrim 60 block damage per hit).\n579\t- **Fail:** the Banner falls, or the builder is KO'd while Gnarlgrim is active. Then \"The Banner has fallen...\" / \"You've come undone...\", and a choice: \"Try again from the start of the siege\" (reload the checkpoint) or \"Return to title\". Waves already cleared stay cleared only within a single attempt.\n580\t- **Sir Buttonsworth** (mini-boss, Button Quarry floor):\n581\t  - Intro: he rises from a heap of buttons.\n582\t  - Moves:\n583\t    - **Slam:** wind .6 s; a shockwave ring of radius 3 blocks expands over .5 s. Jump to avoid it; it deals 12.\n584\t    - **Button Volley:** wind .4 s; 5 buttons in a 50° spread (`E.Bullets`, 110 u/s, 8 damage).\n585\t    - **Stomp Charge:** wind .7 s; charges 140 u/s toward the builder, breaks blocks in its path, and is dizzy for 2 s after hitting a wall. Dizzy takes double damage.\n586\t  - Below 50% HP he summons 3 Lintlings once.\n587\t  - The arena has 4 cobble pillars that break under charges.\n588\t  - Defeat: he pops into buttons and drops the Golden Needle and 3 Steel Thread.\n589\t- **Gnarlgrim the Knotted** (final boss, in and around the Thimbleton plaza), HP 600 in three phases (100–66%, 66–33%, 33–0%):\n590\t  - **Tightly wound.** Def 25, so normal hits do about 1 damage. Mortimer and Granny hint \"Use the Ballistas!\" after 3 such hits.\n591\t  - **Tangled.** 2 manned-ballista hits within 8 s, or 1 hit during his charge, make him Tangled for 5 s: he sits in a heap with `down: .6`, his chest **Heart Knot** glows, and his def drops to 0.\n592\t    - Hits on the Heart Knot (front arc) with the Seam Ripper do ×4, other weapons ×2.\n593\t    - A stagger plays at 100 damage per Tangle; leaving the Tangle triggers a roar knockback.\n594\t  - **Phase 1:** Yarn Slam (ring, radius 3.5) and Tangle Toss (lobbed yarn ball via `E.arc`, landing in 1.1 s on a shadow telegraph; 10 damage and leaves a temporary Tangle block for 20 s).\n595\t  - **Phase 2:** adds Charge (breaks blocks in its path and targets a ballista) and summons 4 Lintlings at the phase start.\n596\t  - **Phase 3:** all moves 25% faster, a double Tangle Toss, and a Knotbrute summon.\n597\t  - Phase transitions: a roar (`shout` expression) and a knockback ring; the music switches to the next layer.\n598\t  - Defeat cutscene: he unravels into heaps of yarn (thread particles) and the Golden Thread fragment flies into the Banner. The rift heals (§7.10).\n599\t\n600\t### 6.13 Day, night, lighting, weather (`DQ.Clock`)\n601\t- One day = `tuning.dayMinutes` (12) real minutes; the story starts on Day 1 at 08:00.\n602\t- **Phases:** dawn 05–07, day 07–17, dusk 17–19, night 19–05.\n603\t- `game.lights.enabled = true` always. `ambient` follows the hour: night .30 with a cool blue tint, dawn and dusk .65 with a warm tint, day 1.0. Use `lights.tint`, setting `lights.dark` per phase, then `lights.refresh()`.\n604\t- Light sources add light pools (§6.7). At night, stars twinkle in the void, Mothlets spawn and Frayed Knights roam the Rift.\n605\t- **HUD clock:** a sun/moon dial with \"Day 3\".\n606\t- **Weather (cosmetic, engine `game.weather`):** the Fraying always has `ash` (purple tint). The Glen rains lightly some days (Day 2 afternoon, Day 4 morning). Weather resets per region when it changes.\n607\t- **Sleeping** is in §6.7. **Night-time Granny line:** the first night she warns \"Monsters get bolder after dark, dearie. A lit room is a safe room!\"\n608\t\n609\t### 6.14 Health and hunger\n610\t- The HUD shows HP as a red patch bar with numbers (\"HP 32/40\") and Belly as a bread-loaf bar.\n611\t- Low HP (< 25%) adds a heartbeat sfx and a red vignette (follows the reduce-flash setting).\n612\t- Food is in §7.3. Eating restores Belly and HP; raw Thimbleberries restore Belly +5.\n613\t- Starving: HP −1 every 4 s, with the prompt \"Your belly is empty! Eat something!\"\n614\t\n615\t### 6.15 Story, quests, dialog, cutscenes (`DQ.Quests`, `DQ.Cutscenes`)\n616\t- **Engine pieces:** `E.Story` (story module) runs conversations as data nodes, with `who`, `say`, `choices`, `set`, `quest`, `done`, `emote` and `event`. One `E.Dialog` instance is skinned as a Dragon Quest-style box: a dark indigo panel with a cream stitched border (dashed 1-px line 2 px inside the edge), a name tab, a portrait at the left, typed text with Animalese blips, and a bobbing arrow sprite at page end (the font has no ▼).\n617\t- **Granny Gossamer's box:** a golden stitched border with gold text and a glowing spool portrait (a custom portrait function).\n618\t- **Text:** 3 lines per page, at most 52 characters per line, `E.font` scale 1 (≈ 31 px tall on a 1080p TV).\n619\t- **Quest data** (§7.10): `{ id, title, giver, steps: [{ text, done: condition }], reward, next, unlock }`. Conditions are data:\n620\t  - `{ have: {item: n} }`, `{ crafted: id }`, `{ placed: objId }`, `{ room: type }`, `{ level: n }`, `{ talk: npc }`\n621\t  - `{ killed: {monster: n} }`, `{ at: poi, radius }`, `{ pattern: id }`, `{ flag: k }`, `{ siegeDone: true }`, `{ boss: id }`\n622\t- **Quest director:** evaluates the current steps on relevant events (cheap) and once per second as a fallback. It advances steps and emits `questStep`/`questDone`. Rewards: `{ cheer, items, notions, flags, heartpatch }`. HUD: \"Quest complete: Wren's Bed\" with a jingle.\n623\t- **Objective tracker** (top centre; switch it off per quest with Track on/off in the Journal, or entirely with the HUD tracker setting): the quest title, the current step text, and a marker. The marker is the engine's `r.marker(x,y,z,{label})`, which becomes an edge arrow off screen, with the distance in blocks. Targets: the POI, NPC or Pattern from the step, or for gather steps the nearest matching plant or block within 40 blocks (scanned once per second).\n624\t- **Cutscenes** are `game.script` generators: camera tweens on a proxy, dialog awaits (`yield E.until(() => !talk.open)`), NPC walks (autopilot), and effects.\n625\t  - Skip: hold ○, Esc or right click for 1 s (a fill ring shows) to jump to the end state.\n626\t  - Every cutscene has `apply()`, which sets its end state. Skipping and tests call it.\n627\t- **Writing style** (Dragon Quest-like):\n628\t  - Short, punchy lines; exclamations; earnest heroism softened with jokes; sewing puns; NPCs with verbal tics.\n629\t  - The silent Builder answers only through choices (\"Of course!\" / \"What's a bed?\")."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7a314112-273a-4f48-a672-e1ae4461860d","uuid":"edc3dac2-57b3-434b-bbfc-2ccd475b0e2a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T05:09:40.394Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261103-220909__x5b1962/work/PLAN.md","content":"### 6.5 Items, bag, hotbar, chests\n- **Bag:** 40 slots, stacks of 99. Key items are separate and unlimited.\n- **Hotbar:** 8 slots that reference item ids in the bag, DQB style. A count of 0 shows a greyed slot. Pickups fill an empty hotbar slot with new placeable or usable items.\n- **Pickups:** broken blocks and defeated monsters drop item entities that bounce out, bob and spin. After 0.3 s they magnetize to a builder within 1.5 blocks and are auto-picked with a \"pickup\" blip. A toast shows \"+3 Straw\" (stacked toasts, bottom right). If the bag is full, the drop stays and the toast says \"Your bag is full!\". Drops despawn after 5 minutes.\n- **Chests:** 20 slots. Interact opens a two-pane screen (bag | chest) with \"Store all materials\".\n- **Town Chest:** from Town Level 2, any chest inside the border can be made the Town Chest (interact → \"Make this the Town Chest\"). Residents put gifts in and take materials out of it for Patterns, and Marigold cooks from it. Exactly one Town Chest exists.\n\n### 6.6 Crafting, stations, Notions\n- **Stations:** Pocket (from the Bag tab \"Pocket Notions\"), Mending Bench, Hearth Pot, Thimble Forge. A station screen lists known recipes for that station.\n  - Each row: icon, name, and ingredients as icons with have/need counts. Have ≥ need shows white with a tick icon, otherwise red with a cross icon (counts in text too, never colour alone). The pixel font has no ✓ or ✗, so draw them as `DQ.Glyphs` icons.\n  - Quantity picker ×1, ×5 or Max. Confirm crafts.\n  - At most 6 rows per page. A large detail pane shows the description.\n- **Crafting feedback:** the builder hammers at the station (a `bash` loop for 0.5 s), sparkles fly, a \"ta-da\" chime plays, and the item's icon pops above the station. Crafted items go into the bag.\n- **Notions** (inspiration). Each recipe has `notion: { on: 'pickup'|'quest'|'level'|'talk'|'start', key }`. The first time the trigger fires:\n  1. The recipe unlocks.\n  2. The builder strikes a thinking pose (a `kneel` blend for 0.4 s, then `'cheer'`).\n  3. A thought bubble shows the item icon above the head for 2 s.\n  4. A harp-gliss jingle plays.\n  5. The popup reads \"**You've got a notion!** Straw Bed. Craft it at a Mending Bench.\"\n  - Popups queue and never overlap.\n  - The Journal's Notions page lists all known recipes.\n\n### 6.7 Objects\nData is in §7.5. Behaviour:\n- **Doors** (2 levels high, 1 cell): they swing open with a tween when a builder or resident is within 1 cell, and close after they leave. Monsters treat closed doors as walls and attack them (door HP 30/50). A broken door drops nothing and breaks the room.\n- **Lights** (torch, lantern, Glow Patch, hearth, forge, banner): each frame, add `game.lights.add(x, y, z+12, radius, intensity, { color })` for lights within the view plus 2 cells. Torch flames come from the engine's shape `flames`. Torches count as room lights.\n- **Beds:** interact at night (19:00–05:00) with no monster within 8 blocks: fade to black, a \"Zzz\" jingle, and time jumps to 06:00. HP is restored, Belly −10, and an autosave runs. During the day: \"It's not bedtime yet!\" Residents use beds at night (§6.10).\n- **Stations:** interact opens crafting. A station must be inside the town border to count for rooms; it works anywhere.\n- **Pin Trap:** a floor object. Monsters on it take 8 damage every 0.8 s and are slowed ×0.6. Builders and residents are unharmed.\n- **Bobbin Ballista** (HP 150):\n  - Unmanned: during a siege it auto-fires at the nearest regular monster within 10 blocks every 5 s (20 damage); it never targets bosses.\n  - Manned (interact):\n    1. The builder sits behind it and the camera eases toward the ballista's facing.\n    2. Stick or mouse aims within ±60°, with aim-assist snapping to the nearest monster in a 12° cone.\n    3. □/LMB fires a spool bolt: 260 u/s, 30 damage, pierces 1. It counts as a *Tangle hit* on Gnarlgrim.\n    4. Reload takes 2.5 s (a crank animation plus a click-clack).\n    5. ○ dismounts.\n  - When destroyed it becomes a \"Broken Ballista\". Interact with 2 Planks to repair it fully.\n- **Bobbin Portals** (prebuilt at POIs): touching one *discovers* it (a jingle and \"Portal attuned: Corduroy Crags\"). Interact opens a travel list of discovered portals: a swirl transition to the destination, ending in front of that portal.\n- **Plants** (tufts, cotton puffs, berry bushes, flowers, puffballs, dead bushes): object-plants that break in one hit with any tool and drop items (§7.3). They regrow at their original spot after 1 in-game day if the cell is still free.\n- **Ancient Buttons** (S3 collectibles): big golden button objects that glint. Interact to collect.\n- **The Banner of Mending:** interact opens the Banner screen: town name, level, a Cheer bar to the next level, the room list, residents and their mood, and the next unlock.\n\n### 6.8 Rooms (`DQ.Rooms`)\n**The rule** (as in the source): a room is an enclosed floor area of **2 to 64 cells**, surrounded on every side by walls **at least 2 blocks high**. It must have **at least one door** in its perimeter and **at least one light** inside. A roof is optional. The room must be inside the town border to count for Cheer, but rooms are detected anywhere so the HUD can say \"Rooms only count inside the town border!\"\n\n**Algorithm** (debounced 0.3 s after any `blockPlaced`, `blockBroken`, `objectPlaced` or `objectRemoved` inside the border + 2 cells):\n1. Collect candidate floor levels L in the region: levels where a cell has solid(L−1) and air at L and L+1, or an object at L that is not a door.\n2. For each L, classify every cell in the region:\n   - WALL: opaque solid blocks at both L and L+1.\n   - DOOR: a door object at L, set in a straight wall: the two cells beside it along the wall are WALL or DOOR. A door on a corner does not count.\n   - FLOOR: not solid at L and L+1, solid below, an object allowed.\n   - OPEN: anything else, including low walls of 1 block and void.\n3. Flood-fill FLOOR cells (4-connected). A component is a room if it:\n   - never reaches an OPEN cell, a region edge or the border;\n   - has a size of 2–64;\n   - touches ≥ 1 DOOR;\n   - contains ≥ 1 light object.\n4. Classify it by the objects on its cells against `DQ.ROOMS`, in priority order. The first match wins; otherwise it is a **Snug**.\n5. Match it to the previous room set by cell overlap ≥ 70%. Emit `roomFormed` (new, or its type changed) and `roomLost`.\n6. **Cheer** is awarded the first time a room of each type forms in a \"slot\". A room's identity is its type plus a hash of its rounded centre, so rebuilding the same room does not pay again; each type pays at most `maxAwards` times (§7.6).\n7. On `roomFormed`: a big centred banner (\"ROOM COMPLETE! Bedroom\") in stitched letters, a fanfare jingle, confetti scraps over the room, and a room-name label floating over its centre for 3 s. Residents react with `cheer` poses.\n\nThe overlay \"Dev → Show rooms\" tints room cells by type and shows OPEN leak cells in red with a cross icon. Use it to explain failures.\n\n**Leak hints:** when a nearly enclosed area fails, the builder looks at the Banner screen or uses Builder's Eye over it. The HUD names the first missing requirement: \"Missing: a door\" / \"a light\" / \"walls must be 2 blocks high\" / \"too big (max 64)\".\n\n### 6.9 Town: Banner, border, Cheer, levels, Patterns (`DQ.Town`)\n- **Planting.** Use the Banner on the marked plaza spot in Thimbleton. That runs a cutscene: the banner rises, a golden light ring expands, and the **border stitch** runs around the town square.\n  - The border is a square of side `2r+1` around the banner, with `r` from §7.7.\n  - On the ground it is an animated dashed running stitch (cream thread, 2-px dashes moving along the edge), drawn at each border cell's surface height.\n  - In the void, at night, it glows faintly.\n- **Cheer sources:** rooms (§7.6), quest rewards, and Cheer bubbles from residents (+5 each, §6.10).\n  - Collecting a bubble: it flies to the HUD banner icon, which pulses, with a two-note \"ding\".\n  - On reaching a level threshold:\n    1. Town Level up (a cutscene of about 4 s): the banner glows, a new stripe stitches itself onto it, and the border grows outward in an animated sweep.\n    2. A popup lists the unlocks.\n    3. The Lv-up jingle plays.\n    4. The next resident arrives at the following dawn (or immediately if it is daytime, walking in from the east road).\n- **Patterns** (blueprints):\n  - **Pattern data:** `{ id, name, size:[w,d,h], layers: [ASCII rows per level], legend: { ch: blockKey | {obj, facing} }, reward }`.\n  - **Placement:** the player uses a Pattern scroll (key item) and a ghost footprint follows the cursor. Turn it 90° with L1/R1 (pad), or the mouse wheel or [ / ] (keyboard); the camera still turns with Q/E and the right stick. Confirm on valid ground inside the border: flat ± 1 level, no objects in the way (blocks in the way are OK; they are shown as \"remove\").\n  - **Ghosts:** each unbuilt cell draws a translucent ghost of its target block (`px.blend(.35)`) with a dashed outline; wrong blocks get a red cross icon. The HUD shows a panel: \"Quilters' Hall: 37/129\", then the materials still needed (have/need, e.g. Cobble 12/35).\n  - **Building:** placing the right block into a ghost cell counts it, with a sparkle and a short arpeggio. Objects in ghost cells (door, lanterns) count the same way.\n  - **Helpers:** residents with the `helper` job (Professor, Wren, and Mortimer by day) take the needed materials from the Town Chest. Each walks to an unbuilt ghost cell they can reach and places a block with a hammer animation and a \"tok\". Rate: `tuning.helperRate` blocks/min each (default 6). If the chest lacks materials, they say so in a balloon (\"Need Planks!\") and idle.\n  - **Completion:** when every cell matches, a celebration cutscene plays (§7.10) and the reward and Cheer are granted. The structure counts as a special room (\"Quilters' Hall\") if its rules match (§7.6).\n\n### 6.10 Residents (`DQ.Residents`)\n- Each resident is a `VoxelBody` plus a `Humanoid` or `Blob` rig, with a profile from `DQ.NPCS` (§7.8): `job`, `schedule`, `needs`, `voice`, `fighter` stats, and dialog nodes.\n- **Schedule** (hours of the day clock; each block picks a target):\n\n  | Time | Activity |\n  |---|---|\n  | 06–08 | Wake, stretch (`wave` pose), go to the plaza |\n  | 08–18 | Job: see below; between tasks, wander inside the border |\n  | 18–20 | Supper: sit at a Mess Hall stool if one exists and eat (+bubble) |\n  | 20–21 | Socialise near the Banner (talk balloons `note`, `dots`) |\n  | 21–06 | Sleep in a free bed in a Bedroom (+bubble at 06:00); without one, sleep on the ground beside the Banner (mood −1, a \"No bed...\" balloon) |\n- **Jobs:**\n  - **Wren** (gatherer): each morning she puts 3 random basics (straw, branch, cotton) into the Town Chest. In sieges she uses a slingshot (4 damage, range 6 blocks, 1.2 s).\n  - **Mortimer** (guard): patrols the border at night with a lantern and fights monsters inside the border with a club (8 damage, `overhead`). In sieges he leads the defence. He needs a Guard Post to stand watch from (+bubble).\n  - **Marigold** (cook): with a Kitchen, cooks at the Hearth Pot (stirring loop) twice a day from Town Chest ingredients into the chest. At 18:00 she sets a dish on the Mess Hall table. In sieges she throws hot pies (5 damage, arc).\n  - **Professor Selvage** (helper): builds Patterns from the Town Chest at the helper rate, or reads in the Workshop. In sieges he hides in the Hall.\n  - **Lintwick** (fluff-farmer): puts 2 Lint into the Town Chest daily and dances (a Blob hop loop) when happy. In sieges he rolls into monsters (3 damage + knockback).\n- **Needs and Cheer bubbles.** At most once per day per need, each satisfied need spawns a floating pink heart bubble (+5 Cheer) over the resident, which stays until collected:\n  - sleep: slept in a bed\n  - meal: ate a dish\n  - comfort: their favourite room exists (Wren: Bedroom, Mortimer: Guard Post, Marigold: Kitchen, Professor: Workshop, Lintwick: a Bedroom with a Felt block in its walls)\n\n  Collect a bubble by walking within 2 blocks of it. Unhappy residents show a `dots` balloon and say why when you talk to them.\n- **Requests:** a resident with an available quest shows a bouncing \"!\" balloon (`story.emote`). Talking starts it, and its steps appear in the Journal and HUD. When the steps are done, a \"?\" balloon shows; talk to them to turn it in.\n- **Arrival cutscene:** the resident walks in along the east road, the camera pans to them, and they say their intro line. \"Mortimer has moved into Thimbleton!\" shows with a jingle.\n- **Navigation** (`DQ.Nav`):\n  - **Graph:** nodes are standable `(x, y, L)`. Edges:\n    - 8-neighbour moves (diagonals only if both orthogonal neighbours are open), cost 1 (diagonal 1.41)\n    - step up 1 level (a hop), cost 2\n    - drop down 1–3 levels, cost 1.5\n    - doors open for residents, closed for monsters\n  - **A\\*** with a binary heap, capped at 3,000 expanded nodes. Smooth paths by line-of-walk. Re-path when an edit touches a path cell.\n  - **Stuck rule:** if a resident has not progressed for 8 s and is off-screen, teleport them to the target. On screen, try a hop, then re-path.\n- **Talk:** dialog with a portrait (`rig.drawPortrait`) and the resident's voice. Lines vary by flags, time of day, mood and town level (`E.Story` nodes with `if` conditions).\n\n### 6.11 Monsters and combat (`DQ.Monsters`, `DQ.Combat`)\n- **AI states:** `idle/wander → notice` (a \"!\" over the head plus a squeak, 0.3 s) `→ chase → windup` (telegraph: flash, crouch or squash, a sound) `→ attack → recover`. Then `→ flee` (below 20% HP for Lintlings) or `→ hurt` (stagger 0.25 s) `→ dead` (pop, particles, drops, `monsterKilled`).\n  - Aggro uses radius `tuning.aggro`, scaled by type (§7.9), plus `world.raycast` sight from eye height.\n  - Leash: return home after chasing 24 blocks away from home.\n- **Spawning:**\n  - Region tables (§7.1) by day or night. Spawn on standable cells under open sky, ≥ 10 blocks from the builder, outside the town border, never inside rooms or during cutscenes.\n  - Rate: 1 spawn per `tuning.spawnEvery` s (day 8, night 5) while the active count is below `tuning.maxMonsters` (default 10).\n  - Despawn: more than 40 blocks away for 20 s.\n- **Damage:**\n  - `dmg = max(1, round((atk − def/2) × U(0.9, 1.1)))`, where U is drawn from the combat stream.\n  - Builder crits: 5%, ×1.5 (Spin Stitch never crits).\n  - Multipliers: `tuning.monsterHp`, `tuning.monsterDmg`, `tuning.builderAtk`, and difficulty (Relaxed 0.5 damage taken, Normal 1, Hard 1.4).\n- **Hit feedback:**\n  - `game.hitFx(x,y,z,{ power, damage, angle })` (hit-stop, shake, impact star, damage number), plus `E.knockback(builder, mon, 120, 40)`.\n  - Monster hits on the builder: knockback 90, i-frames 0.8 s, a red vignette flash under `game.flash` limits.\n  - Each move has its own sound.\n- **Drops:** rolled on death from the drop table (`tuning.dropRate` multiplier on chances); items fly out.\n\n### 6.12 Siege and bosses (`DQ.Siege`, `DQ.Bosses`)\n- **Siege director** (used once in the story, M13–M14, and in the Bee round). It is a `game.script` generator:\n  1. **Prep.** Mortimer's rally line, then a 90 s countdown banner (\"The Knotted army approaches! 1:30\"). Build defences meanwhile; the music turns tense with the drum layer.\n  2. **Autosave checkpoint** `siege`.\n  3. **Waves** W1 → W2 → W3 (§7.9). Each wave spawns over 10 s from the east road (96,76), the Rift (96,80) and the north path (72,52). It ends when all of its monsters are defeated. Between waves: a 25 s breather with \"Wave cleared!\" and a repair prompt.\n  4. **Boss.** Gnarlgrim enters through the Rift (cutscene, §7.10).\n- **Monster targets in sieges:** first the Banner (HP 300; its HP bar is on the HUD during the siege), then ballistas, then the nearest town-structure block in the way (flagged `town` when placed inside the border), then residents, then the builder.\n  - Monsters path with **breaker A\\***: wall blocks count as passable at cost 8 per block, and doors at cost 4.\n  - On reaching a blocking block or door, a monster attacks it (Lintling 3, Pinhog 6, Frayed Knight 8, Knotbrute 25, Gnarlgrim 60 block damage per hit).\n- **Fail:** the Banner falls, or the builder is KO'd while Gnarlgrim is active. Then \"The Banner has fallen...\" / \"You've come undone...\", and a choice: \"Try again from the start of the siege\" (reload the checkpoint) or \"Return to title\". Waves already cleared stay cleared only within a single attempt.\n- **Sir Buttonsworth** (mini-boss, Button Quarry floor):\n  - Intro: he rises from a heap of buttons.\n  - Moves:\n    - **Slam:** wind .6 s; a shockwave ring of radius 3 blocks expands over .5 s. Jump to avoid it; it deals 12.\n    - **Button Volley:** wind .4 s; 5 buttons in a 50° spread (`E.Bullets`, 110 u/s, 8 damage).\n    - **Stomp Charge:** wind .7 s; charges 140 u/s toward the builder, breaks blocks in its path, and is dizzy for 2 s after hitting a wall. Dizzy takes double damage.\n  - Below 50% HP he summons 3 Lintlings once.\n  - The arena has 4 cobble pillars that break under charges.\n  - Defeat: he pops into buttons and drops the Golden Needle and 3 Steel Thread.\n- **Gnarlgrim the Knotted** (final boss, in and around the Thimbleton plaza), HP 600 in three phases (100–66%, 66–33%, 33–0%):\n  - **Tightly wound.** Def 25, so normal hits do about 1 damage. Mortimer and Granny hint \"Use the Ballistas!\" after 3 such hits.\n  - **Tangled.** 2 manned-ballista hits within 8 s, or 1 hit during his charge, make him Tangled for 5 s: he sits in a heap with `down: .6`, his chest **Heart Knot** glows, and his def drops to 0.\n    - Hits on the Heart Knot (front arc) with the Seam Ripper do ×4, other weapons ×2.\n    - A stagger plays at 100 damage per Tangle; leaving the Tangle triggers a roar knockback.\n  - **Phase 1:** Yarn Slam (ring, radius 3.5) and Tangle Toss (lobbed yarn ball via `E.arc`, landing in 1.1 s on a shadow telegraph; 10 damage and leaves a temporary Tangle block for 20 s).\n  - **Phase 2:** adds Charge (breaks blocks in its path and targets a ballista) and summons 4 Lintlings at the phase start.\n  - **Phase 3:** all moves 25% faster, a double Tangle Toss, and a Knotbrute summon.\n  - Phase transitions: a roar (`shout` expression) and a knockback ring; the music switches to the next layer.\n  - Defeat cutscene: he unravels into heaps of yarn (thread particles) and the Golden Thread fragment flies into the Banner. The rift heals (§7.10).\n\n### 6.13 Day, night, lighting, weather (`DQ.Clock`)\n- One day = `tuning.dayMinutes` (12) real minutes; the story starts on Day 1 at 08:00.\n- **Phases:** dawn 05–07, day 07–17, dusk 17–19, night 19–05.\n- `game.lights.enabled = true` always. `ambient` follows the hour: night .30 with a cool blue tint, dawn and dusk .65 with a warm tint, day 1.0. Use `lights.tint`, setting `lights.dark` per phase, then `lights.refresh()`.\n- Light sources add light pools (§6.7). At night, stars twinkle in the void, Mothlets spawn and Frayed Knights roam the Rift.\n- **HUD clock:** a sun/moon dial with \"Day 3\".\n- **Weather (cosmetic, engine `game.weather`):** the Fraying always has `ash` (purple tint). The Glen rains lightly some days (Day 2 afternoon, Day 4 morning). Weather resets per region when it changes.\n- **Sleeping** is in §6.7. **Night-time Granny line:** the first night she warns \"Monsters get bolder after dark, dearie. A lit room is a safe room!\"\n\n### 6.14 Health and hunger\n- The HUD shows HP as a red patch bar with numbers (\"HP 32/40\") and Belly as a bread-loaf bar.\n- Low HP (< 25%) adds a heartbeat sfx and a red vignette (follows the reduce-flash setting).\n- Food is in §7.3. Eating restores Belly and HP; raw Thimbleberries restore Belly +5.\n- Starving: HP −1 every 4 s, with the prompt \"Your belly is empty! Eat something!\"\n\n### 6.15 Story, quests, dialog, cutscenes (`DQ.Quests`, `DQ.Cutscenes`)\n- **Engine pieces:** `E.Story` (story module) runs conversations as data nodes, with `who`, `say`, `choices`, `set`, `quest`, `done`, `emote` and `event`. One `E.Dialog` instance is skinned as a Dragon Quest-style box: a dark indigo panel with a cream stitched border (dashed 1-px line 2 px inside the edge), a name tab, a portrait at the left, typed text with Animalese blips, and a bobbing arrow sprite at page end (the font has no ▼).\n- **Granny Gossamer's box:** a golden stitched border with gold text and a glowing spool portrait (a custom portrait function).\n- **Text:** 3 lines per page, at most 52 characters per line, `E.font` scale 1 (≈ 31 px tall on a 1080p TV).\n- **Quest data** (§7.10): `{ id, title, giver, steps: [{ text, done: condition }], reward, next, unlock }`. Conditions are data:\n  - `{ have: {item: n} }`, `{ crafted: id }`, `{ placed: objId }`, `{ room: type }`, `{ level: n }`, `{ talk: npc }`\n  - `{ killed: {monster: n} }`, `{ at: poi, radius }`, `{ pattern: id }`, `{ flag: k }`, `{ siegeDone: true }`, `{ boss: id }`\n- **Quest director:** evaluates the current steps on relevant events (cheap) and once per second as a fallback. It advances steps and emits `questStep`/`questDone`. Rewards: `{ cheer, items, notions, flags, heartpatch }`. HUD: \"Quest complete: Wren's Bed\" with a jingle.\n- **Objective tracker** (top centre; switch it off per quest with Track on/off in the Journal, or entirely with the HUD tracker setting): the quest title, the current step text, and a marker. The marker is the engine's `r.marker(x,y,z,{label})`, which becomes an edge arrow off screen, with the distance in blocks. Targets: the POI, NPC or Pattern from the step, or for gather steps the nearest matching plant or block within 40 blocks (scanned once per second).\n- **Cutscenes** are `game.script` generators: camera tweens on a proxy, dialog awaits (`yield E.until(() => !talk.open)`), NPC walks (autopilot), and effects.\n  - Skip: hold ○, Esc or right click for 1 s (a fill ring shows) to jump to the end state.\n  - Every cutscene has `apply()`, which sets its end state. Skipping and tests call it.\n- **Writing style** (Dragon Quest-like):\n  - Short, punchy lines; exclamations; earnest heroism softened with jokes; sewing puns; NPCs with verbal tics.\n  - The silent Builder answers only through choices (\"Of course!\" / \"What's a bed?\").","numLines":200,"startLine":430,"totalLines":1675}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01C7WsXRFtDvcq1jjKyQYkUx","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
