{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014iW7WrjRxMyFm9eh7CLQhg","type":"tool_result","content":"430:- `r.shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: Queue a shape standing at (x, y, z), feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor: r.shape(id | entry, x, y, z, o). o: { facing (radians, where its front points; default PI/2, south, as written), scale, mats: { slot: material }, flip (mirror it x to -x be\n767:- `map.solid(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})` †: make a shape solid in this map: map.solid(id | entry, x, y, z, o) with r.shape's placement (facing, scale, flip, params) -> the solid ({ x, y (the footprint's middle), z, top, hx, hy, c, s, shape, px, py (where it was placed) }; map.solids holds them; wh\n860:- `level.move(b, dt, solids)`: Move a body { x, z, vx, vz, w, h } (x = center, z = feet, vz > 0 = up) by its velocity, colliding with the level. Sets b.onGround, b.onOneWay, b.hitWall (-1 left, 1 right, 0), b.hitCeiling, b.bumped ({ cx, cz, id } of a ceiling tile hit from below, for ? blocks and\n885:- `hero.update(dt, level, ctl = {}, solids)`: move it one step: ctl is game.input or an intent { x: -1..1, jump, jumpPressed, up, down, dash } (enemies, bots); solids: moving platforms [{ x, z, w, h, vx, vz }] to stand on\n1099:- `E.shapeMesh(id, o = {})`: a shape's triangles, for a 3D renderer (the 3D engine's world.shape): E.shapeMesh(id | entry, { params, mats, seg }) -> { groups: [{ mat, key, lid, curved, face, pos, nrm, uv }], bounds [x0, y0, z0, x1, y1, z1] } in the entry's own units and frame (z up, its front +\n1102:- `E.shapeSprite(id, o = {})`: a shape as a sprite (E.sprite's kind: r.sprite, px.sprite, inventories, HUDs, portraits): E.shapeSprite(id, { view: 'iso', facing, size (its scale, 1), mats, params, outline: true | a color | false }). The view is a name or a View, as given (r.shape draws steep vi\n1503:- `mode7.shape(id, x, y, z = 0, o = {})`: gather one of the engine's shapes (r.shape's: 'barrel', 'tree', ...; the full engine), seen from the camera's side at its distance's size: o.facing (radians), o.size (1)\n104:- 1646 Module story: dialogue as data, flags and values, a quest log and emote balloons (engine/modules/story.js); E.Story: story\n228:- `view.set(yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1)`: change the angles and scale in place (game.setView and rotateView use their own copies); returns the view\n483:- `game.hitFx(x, y, z, o = {})`: everything a good hit needs in one call: hit-stop, shake, an impact star, sparks along the hit direction, a sound, a damage number and a rumble on a gamepad. hitFx\n485:- `game.mouseGround()`: mouse position on the ground (world units), or null\n492:- `game.resetCamera()` †: undo setZoom and rotateView: the scene's own zoom again (camera.start, or camera.tall on a screen held upright; 1 without), no turn. The player's zoom stays (settings.zoo\n494:- `game.rotateView(deg)` †: turn the camera around the vertical axis in ground views: game.rotateView(45) (degrees). Side views never turn\n498:- `game.setZoom(z)` †: camera zoom on top of the view: game.setZoom(1.5) (.5 .. 3), the game's own; where the scene lets the player zoom (camera.zoom), theirs multiplies it (game.zoom is the two t\n557:- `game.yaw = 0` †: its turn in degrees on top of the view (rotateView)\n558:- `game.zoom = 1` †: the camera's zoom now (1 = as the view is): the game's (setZoom, a scene's camera.start) times the player's (settings.zoom: the wheel, a pinch), within the scene's camera.zoom\n1287:- `click.story` †: the E.Story that talks (or null)\n1648:- `new E.Story(game, o = {}) → story`: new E.Story(game, { people, nodes, vars, on, dialog }): the talk of a game (the manual above)\n1656:- `story.run(id, o = {})`: start node id (stopping any other); o.onDone(story) when it ends\n1670:- `story.running = false`: a node runs","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7a314112-273a-4f48-a672-e1ae4461860d","uuid":"181f5b1b-171f-479f-a543-a23de8974686","timestamp":"2026-11-04T0