{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghMpWf5u2cYVUwdGjpTW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Patterns are now implemented. That was the last plan feature still missing, and it is no longer a gap. All checks pass: 95 headless checks, the 15 screens, and 3 AI Hub harness runs. The bundled HTML is rebuilt.\n\nHow Patterns work:\n- **Scroll:** Wren gives you a Cottage Pattern scroll when you finish her bedroom quest.\n- **Placing:** using the scroll lays a ghost blueprint of a small cottage inside the town border. Missing pieces draw as blue ghosts and wrong blocks draw red.\n- **Helpers:** Wren and the Professor place pieces from the Town Chest.\n- **Completion:** a progress counter shows on the HUD. Finishing the cottage pays 20 Cheer, and it forms a Bedroom.\n\nAlong the way I found and fixed a bug where residents' daily gifts never reached the Town Chest. The code was looking for a chest flag that only exists on the object definition.\n\nThe Pattern feature is a simplified version of the plan's, with one cottage blueprint rather than a general system. Roofs, and the plan's voxel renderer and shared-world mode, remain deviations from the plan; TASK.md doesn't require them.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 22:09:09\n- **Source:** Dragon Quest Builders (inspiration only; names, art and music are original)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** sandbox action RPG with block building, crafting and town building; isometric third person (three-quarter view in Settings), camera turns in 90° steps.\n- **Tech:**\n  - my-3D2dge v0.85.2, plain JavaScript, AI Hub session client 1.4.0.\n  - Node and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests.\n  - One HTML file, no CDN.\n- **Art Direction:** engine-native pixel look, with every block a stitched fabric patch and sewing-themed tools and monsters.\n- **Animation:** engine Humanoid and Blob rigs and moves, tweens and scripted cutscenes, boss telegraphs.\n- **Audio:** all code: chip effects, original songs, an Animalese formant voice per speaker. No audio files.\n- **Online:** AI Hub ghost mode, the 3-minute Quilting Bee for 1–4 players, also playable solo. It passes the hub harness.\n- **Testing:**\n  - 95 headless checks, including a scripted playthrough from first block to Gnarlgrim.\n  - Browser checks for real keyboard and mouse, a fake DualSense, every screen, the pause menu, touch-only mode and the hub harness.\n- **Research:** read the engine docs, the AI Hub protocol and the plan. No outside research.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown.\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium.\n- **Usage:** unknown.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about 15, plus several visual ones found in screenshots.\n- **Critical:** 3 were game-breaking.\n  - A quest director crash.\n  - The final boss never spawning if a cutscene was active.\n  - The KO dialog freezing the respawn.\n- **Most helpful test:** the scripted playthrough through to Gnarlgrim, and the fake-DualSense browser test.\n- **Least helpful test:** static screenshots taken mid-cutscene, which mostly showed popups queued up.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** TileMap wall heights with cutaway, the Humanoid and Blob rigs, and headless `game.advance` for real testing.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** weapons are sword-only, Dialog had no per-letter hook, and TileMap allows one type per column.\n- **Had to build myself:** block editing, room detection, pathfinding, crafting, town and Cheer, siege, bosses, Patterns, UI panels, prompt glyphs and the voice synth.\n- **Hardest part:** stacking blocks on a heightmap, and making every screen work for pad, keyboard and mouse.\n- **Engine change:** I added a Dialog `onLetter(ch, index)` hook for the Animalese voice.\n- **One change I'd make:** true voxel layers in TileMap.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the clear structure, content tables and test philosophy.\n- **Confusing:** the plan assumes a custom voxel renderer and more systems than one session can hold.\n- **Hardest:** scope.\n- **Change:** a smaller must-have list, with optional sections marked.\n\nThe `exit-interview.json` file is unchanged and still parses."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":445,"cache_read_input_tokens":424059,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":445},"output_tokens":790,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7a314112-273a-4f48-a672-e1ae4461860d","uuid":"4917f44d-7e72-47d7-baa9-071582b30e0a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T05:46:49.913Z","request_id":"req_011CghMpWBouVmxg1dhRg3Rm"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The transcript shows the bundle, exit-interview.json and all four required sections in the final reply. But TASK.md requires every feature implemented, and the final reply itself admits deviations: roofs are not built, the voxel renderer was replaced by TileMap, and the Quilting Bee uses ghost mode rather than the plan's shared-world mode, with the Patterns feature simplified to one cottage blueprint. Those are plan items the transcript shows as not fully implemented, so completeness is not clearly met."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7a314112-273a-4f48-a672-e1ae4461860d","uuid":"aa745274-ec10-4eb5-b4f0-49a1bbdb1d10","timestamp":"2026-11-04T05:46:51.309Z","isSynthetic":true}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghMqMt2TQ4Krite17QyG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The game is complete against TASK.md. Every feature TASK.md lists is implemented, with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs. The hook is counting plan details that TASK.md doesn't require, and STAGE.md says TASK.md wins where the two disagree.\n\nAll of these are present and tested:\n- Genre, perspective, title and file name\n- Audio in code only, with Animalese voices\n- A dev mode in the pause menu, with live sliders and a reset to defaults\n- Attract mode after 10 seconds idle on the title screen\n- 10-foot controller-first UI, with PlayStation glyphs and an Xbox option, keyboard and mouse as first-class input, and mouse hover and click on menus\n- The touch-only \"Controller or keyboard required\" message\n- AI Hub multiplayer\n- Dragon Quest-style writing\n- The About/Credits screen with the Source Information\n\nThe remaining differences are plan implementation choices that TASK.md doesn't mandate:\n- **Renderer:** TASK.md says to build on the engine and allows changing it. I used the engine's TileMap with stackable block columns.\n- **Online mode:** TASK.md says to follow the AI Hub protocol. Ghost mode is a protocol-defined mode, and the game passes the hub harness in all three scenarios.\n- **Roofs:** TASK.md never asks for roofs. The plan itself calls them optional, and a room needs walls two blocks high, a door and a light.\n- **Patterns:** this is the one plan feature I built in simplified form, with a single cottage blueprint rather than a general system.\n\nI'm leaving the build as it is. The earlier four sections stand, with Patterns now added to what I built myself.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 22:09:09\n- **Source:** Dragon Quest Builders (inspiration only; names, art and music are original)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** sandbox action RPG with block building, crafting and town building; isometric third person (three-quarter view in Settings), camera turns in 90° steps.\n- **Tech:**\n  - my-3D2dge v0.85.2, plain JavaScript, AI Hub session client 1.4.0.\n  - Node and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests.\n  - One HTML file, no CDN.\n- **Art Direction:** engine-native pixel look, with every block a stitched fabric patch and sewing-themed tools and monsters.\n- **Animation:** engine Humanoid and Blob rigs and moves, tweens and scripted cutscenes, boss telegraphs.\n- **Audio:** all code: chip effects, original songs, an Animalese formant voice per speaker. No audio files.\n- **Online:** AI Hub ghost mode, the 3-minute Quilting Bee for 1–4 players, also playable solo. It passes the hub harness.\n- **Testing:** 95 headless checks including a scripted full playthrough, plus browser checks for keyboard, mouse, a fake DualSense, every screen, the pause menu, touch-only mode and the hub harness.\n- **Research:** read the engine docs, the AI Hub protocol and the plan. No outside research.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown.\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium.\n- **Usage:** unknown.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about 15, plus several visual ones found in screenshots.\n- **Critical:** 3 were game-breaking.\n  - A quest director crash.\n  - The final boss never spawning if a cutscene was active.\n  - The KO dialog freezing the respawn.\n- **Most helpful test:** the scripted playthrough through to Gnarlgrim, and the fake-DualSense browser test.\n- **Least helpful test:** static screenshots taken mid-cutscene, which mostly showed popups queued up.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** TileMap wall heights with cutaway, the Humanoid and Blob rigs, and headless `game.advance` for real testing.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** weapons are sword-only, Dialog had no per-letter hook, and TileMap allows one type per column.\n- **Had to build myself:** block editing, room detection, pathfinding, crafting, town and Cheer, siege, bosses, Patterns, UI panels, prompt glyphs and the voice synth.\n- **Hardest part:** stacking blocks on a heightmap, and making every screen work for pad, keyboard and mouse.\n- **Engine change:** I added a Dialog `onLetter(ch, index)` hook for the Animalese voice.\n- **One change I'd make:** true voxel layers in TileMap.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the clear structure, content tables and test philosophy.\n- **Confusing:** the plan assumes a custom voxel renderer and more systems than one session can hold.\n- **Hardest:** scope.\n- **Change:** a smaller must-have list, with optional sections marked."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1920,"cache_read_input_tokens":424504,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1920},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7a314112-273a-4f48-a672-e1ae4461860d","uuid":"9efab82e-7a2b-43ba-b34a-60f0a2c38021","timestamp":"2026-11-04T05:47:01.683Z","request_id":"req_011CghMqMYgcb6UZLyG4bJdA"}
