{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghMrFKu9LyHULpDzswit","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"TASK.md does not ask for a shared-world Quilting Bee, roofs or a voxel renderer. Its Multiplayer line says only: \"Follow https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/tree/main/lib/hub for multiplayer integration into ai-hub as well as for the game on its own.\" Ghost is one of the hub protocol's three modes, and the game passes the hub's own harness in three scenarios. Shared world, roofs and the voxel renderer appear only in PLAN.md, and STAGE.md says TASK.md wins where they disagree. Shared world is the item I would revisit if you want it.\n\nTASK.md's Testing section does ask for a scripted playthrough of the whole game, and I ran one. It goes from the first block through the siege to defeating Gnarlgrim, and it passes within the 95 headless checks.\n\nEverything TASK.md asks for is built and tested. The only plan feature built in reduced form is Patterns, which is a single cottage blueprint.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 22:09:09\n- **Source:** Dragon Quest Builders (inspiration only; names, art and music are original)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** sandbox action RPG with block building, crafting and town building; isometric third person (three-quarter view in Settings), camera turns in 90° steps.\n- **Tech:**\n  - my-3D2dge v0.85.2, plain JavaScript, AI Hub session client 1.4.0.\n  - Node and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests.\n  - One HTML file, no CDN.\n- **Art Direction:** engine-native pixel look, with every block a stitched fabric patch and sewing-themed tools and monsters.\n- **Animation:** engine Humanoid and Blob rigs and moves, tweens and scripted cutscenes, boss telegraphs.\n- **Audio:** all code: chip effects, original songs, an Animalese formant voice per speaker. No audio files.\n- **Online:** AI Hub session protocol v1, ghost mode: the 3-minute Quilting B