{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghMsuCEvs7tjnxAkFHwe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"TASK.md does not ask for a shared AI Hub round, and I'm not building one. Its Multiplayer line only says to follow the `lib/hub` protocol for integration, and ghost mode is one of the protocol's three defined modes. The game passes the hub's own harness in ghost mode, which is the hub's test for this integration. \"Shared world\" appears only in PLAN.md. Where the plan goes beyond TASK.md's wording, STAGE.md says TASK.md wins.\n\nI also never described Patterns as missing. It is implemented and tested (laying out the ghost, wrong and right blocks, helper residents building from the Town Chest, the Cheer payout). The blueprint is a single cottage layout, but TASK.md names no Pattern requirement beyond the game being feature-complete.\n\nIf you want shared-world mode, tell me. It's a new build, well beyond TASK.md's wording.\n\nFinal state: the bundled HTML is in the folder root and `exit-interview.json` parses with every field filled. All 95 headless checks (including the scripted full playthrough), the 15 screens and the 3 hub harness runs passed on the last full run.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 22:09:09\n- **Source:** Dragon Quest Builders (inspiration only; names, art and music are original)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** sandbox action RPG with block building, crafting and town building; isometric third person (three-quarter view in Settings), camera turns in 90° steps.\n- **Tech:**\n  - my-3D2dge v0.85.2, plain JavaScript, AI Hub session client 1.4.0.\n  - Node and Playwright 1.63.0 for tests.\n  - One HTML file, no CDN.\n- **Art Direction:** engine-native pixel look, with every block a stitched fabric patch and sewing-themed tools and monsters.\n- **Animation:** engine Humanoid and Blob rigs and moves, tweens and scripted cutscenes, boss telegraphs.\n- **Audio:** all code: chip effects, original songs, an Animalese formant voice per speaker. No audio files.\n- **Online:** AI Hub session protocol v1, ghost mode: the 3-minute Quilting Bee for 1–4 players, also playable solo.\n- **Testing:** 95 headless checks including the scripted full playthrough, plus browser checks for keyboard, mouse, a fake DualSense, every screen, the pause menu, touch-only mode and the hub harness.\n- **Research:** read the engine docs, the AI Hub protocol and the plan. No outside research.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown.\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium.\n- **Usage:** unknown.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about 15, plus several visual ones found in screenshots.\n- **Critical:** 3 were game-breaking.\n  - A quest director crash.\n  - The final boss never spawning if a cutscene was active.\n  - The KO dialog freezing the respawn.\n- **Most helpful test:** the scripted playthrough through to Gnarlgrim, and the fake-DualSense browser test.\n- **Least helpful test:** static screenshots taken mid-cutscene, which mostly showed popups queued up.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** TileMap wall heights with cutaway, the Humanoid and Blob rigs, and headless `game.advance` for real testing.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** weapons are sword-only, Dialog had no per-letter hook, and TileMap allows one type per column.\n- **Had to build myself:** block editing, room detection, pathfinding, crafting, town and Cheer, siege, bosses, Patterns, UI panels, prompt glyphs and the voice synth.\n- **Hardest part:** stacking blocks on a heightmap, and making every screen work for pad, keyboard and mouse.\n- **Engine change:** I added a Dialog `onLetter(ch, index)` hook for the Animalese voice.\n- **One change I'd make:** true voxel layers in TileMap.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the clear structure, content tables and test philosophy.\n- **Confusing:** the plan assumes a custom voxel renderer and more systems than one session can hold.\n- **Hardest:** scope.\n- **Change:** a smaller must-have list, with optional sections marked."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2018,"cache_read_input_tokens":430430,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2018},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7a314112-273a-4f48-a672-e1ae4461860d","uuid":"11a648bd-430e-4473-b47f-0a0a8ba56767","timestamp":"2026-11-04T05:47:36.258Z","request_id":"req_011CghMstpRCXLTKRyV5oCsJ"}
